{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Let us pass, we pray you, through your land.</b> You have no grounds to contest the inheritance of the land of Israel, just as you have not paid the debt." "<b>We will not pass through field or vineyard.</b> That we would not destroy them. <b>And we will not drink water of a well.</b> Not even water of cisterns will we drink — this is its plain sense. And its Midrash: we will not drink even water of our own well, and we will buy from you." "<b>The king's highway we will go.</b> The road that the king travels on, or the road that the king — who is the king of Edom — commands." "<b>Until we pass your border.</b> He did not say 'until we come to the land,' even though that was the intention, for he feared to mention the land to him, lest the king of Edom say: Jacob their father came with deception and took my birthright and my blessing — had it not been so, the land would have been mine. But with Sihon he specified the land and mentioned it explicitly."], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:34:19.054550821Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}